console.log(person2.age); // 25
```
In both cases, the resulting object has properties `name` and `age`, but they are set up differently.

Now, what about functions? In JavaScript, functions are first-class citizens, which means that they can be assigned to variables, passed as arguments to other functions, and returned from functions. Functions can also be used as constructors, as shown in the example above.

